      en: ["Architect: Designed in 1924 by the visionary Alexander Tamanian", "Size: The square covers an area of approximately 30,000 m2", "Material: Constructed using distinct pink and white volcanic tufa", "Fountains: The Singing Fountains were first installed in 1970", "Former name: Known as Lenin Square until Armenia's independence in 1991", "Layout: Comprises an oval-shaped core and a trapezoidal open area"],
